#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc7c3a73-c051-5320-b6d9-d1c742969358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334888} {:answer/id #uuid "322f90ee-5a4e-5818-a81e-012433718bab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc7c3a73-c051-5320-b6d9-d1c742969358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334888} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8d4e799-d540-5a73-9421-bb3f497c6e73" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334887}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c1e61923-44f8-5da3-a12f-75078d76a376" :question/math-academy-id "q-280521" :question/problem "A delivery drone starts from the point with position vector $(1i+2j)\\,\\text{mi}$ and moves with a constant velocity of $(3i-2j)\\,\\text{mi/h}.$ Determine the distance $(|r|)$ from the drone to the origin after $3$ hours.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{mi}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant velocity $u,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut,\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=1i+2j,\\,u=3i-2j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the drone after $t=3\\,\\text{h}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & ={r}_{0}+ut \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(3i-2j)(3) \\\\  & =(1i+2j)+(9i-6j) \\\\  & =(10i-4j)\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the drone to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|10i-4j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{116} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{29}\\,\\text{mi}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186334890 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Particle and the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f32853f3-7831-534b-9a86-e6e5de0b1675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f32853f3-7831-534b-9a86-e6e5de0b1675" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334892} :answer-field/id #uuid "d46554d1-c8b7-57c6-8146-1442fe9a4719" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186334891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bcb455c9-26c8-584d-bb4c-1f9bcb5b3690" :question/math-academy-id "q-280533" :question/problem "An object moves from the origin with an acceleration of $(-2i+4j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i+j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the distance from the object to the origin$(|r|)$ after $2$ seconds.\n\n$\\,|r|=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m}$" :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=0i+0j,\\,u=3i+j,\\,a=-2i+4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the object after $t=2\\,\\text{s}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(0i+0j)+(3i+j)(2)+\\frac{1}{2}(-2i+4j)(2)^{2} \\\\  & =(6i+2j)+\\frac{1}{2}(-8i+16j) \\\\  & =(6i+2j)+(-4i+8j) \\\\  & =(2i+10j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the object to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|2i+10j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{104} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{26}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
